# Caddy snippet for deployments WITHOUT origin-side Cloudflare Access validation
# (CF_ACCESS_MODE=off, the default). Imported by ../Caddyfile inside the site
# block, where it contributes no directives at all.
#
# Use this mode when:
#   * the stack runs on a home/LAN network, where there is no Cloudflare Access
#     application in front of it - requiring an Access JWT there would lock
#     everybody (including you) out of the site, or
#   * the site is opened to the general public and the Access application is
#     switched off. Because this is a separate switch from TLS_MODE, going public
#     needs no certificate, DNS or image change: set CF_ACCESS_MODE=off in .env
#     and restart Caddy.
#
# This file intentionally contains only comments: Caddy imports it and finds no
# tokens to add to the site block, so the request handling is unchanged.